(D5 — Discrepancy 5 repro: a DECLARED `float` or `map` return type is lost
 when the call result is printed directly rather than routed through a
 declared variable. The float prints as its IEEE-754 bit pattern
 (4612811918334230528 = 0x4004000000000000 = 2.5) and the map as a raw
 heap address; the same two values print correctly one line earlier, out
 of variables of the declared type. text, boolean and list are unaffected
 (FUN-40). This is the shape of vox bug #45, except that #45 says
 declaring the return type is the cure — here it is declared and the
 result is still wrong. The map address varies per run (ASLR), so this
 probe is compared on its EXIT CODE only: it exits 3 unconditionally
 after printing.
